		)
		(uuid "3c9c6f71-4c70-4d08-a9c1-fee3e756d1d1")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\n3V3 LDO total current needs to be lower than 5mA at startup:\nEEPROM read: 1mA\nPOWER OK LED: 0.65mA\nTPD4S480: 0.16mA\nLM2765: 0.13mA\nLTC7004: 0.05mA\nI²C pull-ups: ~~0.5mA\nADC resistors: 0.02mA\nAND gate: <0.01mA\nTotal ~~2.5mA < 5mA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 31.75 45.72 0)
		(size 52.705 33.655)
		(margins 2.25 2.25 2.25 2.25)
		(stroke
			(width 1.27)
			(type solid)
			(color 255 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(color 255 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "49ff3c88-c51b-46b6-8988-db302e398329")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nThe default state for a USB-C port (before or during negotiation, or if negotiation fails) is effectively USB 2.0 specs: 5V @ 500mA. Therefore we want to limit the inrush current. Synapticon drives have an averager of 150uF of input capacitance. As explained in application informations of LTC7004, the gate capacitor and  TGUP resistors are chosen to limit the current to a safe limit of arround 250mA.\n\nI_inrush = (0.7x12Vx150uF)/(50kOhm x 100nF) = 252mA                                                      Time to reach 48V = (150uF x 48) / 0.252A = 29ms\n\nBoost capacitor adjustments:   SQJB90EP has a max gate charge of 2x25nC = 50nC\nThe relationship for CB that needs to be maintained when CG is used is given by: Cb > (mosfet Qg)/1V + 10 x CG = 1.05 uF\nWith derating, a 2.2uF cap is necessary.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.085 15.875 0)
		(size 105.41 22.86)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
		(stroke
			(width 1)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.143 1.143)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "57356839-faa1-435b-932c-ecbd51726ae4")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nLED current:\n(3.3 - 2.65)/330 = 2mA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 374.015 159.385 0)
		(size 27.94 9.525)
		(margins 2 2 2 2)
